    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment on owner creation with minimal structural impact \u2014 adding behaviour as a small, self-contained function rather than growing any existing method.\n\n**New cohesive unit** (`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`): a single-method OfficeFloor function that reads the built `Owner`, computes `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` + a global 4-digit sequence = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`), and mutates the entity in place \u2014 following the existing `EnsureOwnerTelephoneUnique` pattern (WMC_other = 0, CC = 1).\n\n**Wiring / plumbing** (each a minimal edit):\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step between `ensureUniqueTelephone` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `customerCode` field with a trivial getter/setter (CC 1 each).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct auto-maps the same-named field, so no mapper change).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (placed last so the positional seed inserts only needed a trailing `NULL`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes (`SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes with consecutive sequence numbers), and the full suite is green.",
